abstract: >-
  An evidence-driven Quality Engineering framework for evaluating
  Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems across retrieval quality, context
  quality, groundedness, hallucination, citation integrity, security,
  authorization, latency, cost, stability and regression quality. The work
  advocates deterministic-first evaluation, versioned datasets, traceable
  evidence, adversarial testing and CI/CD quality gates.